# rule.forbid.integration.mocks

## .what
integration (`.integration.test.ts`) and acceptance (`.acceptance.test.ts`) tests must not mock. a mocked integration verifies only the mock

## .why
mocks drift from real behavior → false confidence → prod fails while tests pass

## .exception
mock only where clearly unavoidable (severe rate limit, prohibitive cost, no sandbox), documented inline at the mock:
```ts
/**
 * .mock = github api
 * .why = rate limit would exhaust quota in ci
 * .real = github.real.integration.test.ts, run before release
 */
jest.mock('@/access/sdks/sdkGithub');
```

## .credentials
absent credential → fail fast with ConstraintError + hint (`rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath --env test`). never skip silently, never fake it

## .enforcement
- undocumented mock (`jest.mock()` with no inline .mock/.why/.real) = blocker
- silent credential bypass = blocker

## .see also
rule.forbid.acceptance.mocks (same rule, acceptance scope) · rule.require.acceptance.blackbox · rule.forbid.unit.remote-boundaries
